            {"num": 2, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_RTC/AP_RTC.h', "lines": '32-40', "line_start": 32, "line_end": 40, "function": 'AP_RTC::get_utc_usec()', "role": 'Source', "code_snippet": '    /*\n      get clock in UTC microseconds.  Returns false if it is not available.\n     */\n    bool get_utc_usec(uint64_t &usec) const;\n\n    // set the system time.  If the time has already been set by\n    // something better (according to source_type), this set will be\n    // ignored.\n    void set_utc_usec(uint64_t time_utc_usec, source_type type);', "notes": 'UTC wall-clock time in microseconds (returns false if unavailable). The absolute-time API consumed for logging and GPS-time conversion.'},
            {"num": 3, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_RTC/AP_RTC.cpp', "lines": '56-65', "line_start": 56, "line_end": 65, "function": 'AP_RTC::set_utc_usec()', "role": 'Transform', "code_snippet": "    // only allow time to be moved forward from the same sourcetype\n    // while the vehicle is disarmed:\n    if (hal.util->get_soft_armed()) {\n        if (type >= rtc_source_type) {\n            // e.g. system-time message when we've been set by the GPS\n            return;\n        }\n    } else {\n        // vehicle is disarmed; accept (e.g.) GPS time source updates\n        if (type > rtc_source_type) {", "notes": 'Time-SOURCE ARBITRATION: accepts a new UTC time only if its source_type out-ranks the current rtc_source_type (GPS > GCS > HW). Selects the best clock source.'},
            {"num": 4, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_RTC/JitterCorrection.cpp', "lines": '50-58', "line_start": 50, "line_end": 58, "function": 'JitterCorrection::correct_offboard_timestamp_usec()', "role": 'Transform', "code_snippet": "uint64_t JitterCorrection::correct_offboard_timestamp_usec(uint64_t offboard_usec, uint64_t local_usec)\n{\n    int64_t diff_us = int64_t(local_usec) - int64_t(offboard_usec);\n\n    if (!initialised ||\n        diff_us < link_offset_usec) {\n        // this message arrived from the remote system with a\n        // timestamp that would imply the message was from the\n        // future. We know that isn't possible, so we adjust down the", "notes": "Time synchronization: maps an offboard (remote-system) timestamp onto the local clock by tracking the minimum observed link offset — rejects 'from the future' samples."},
            {"num": 5, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_Scheduler/AP_Scheduler.cpp', "lines": '354-363', "line_start": 354, "line_end": 363, "function": 'AP_Scheduler::loop()', "role": 'Transform', "code_snippet": '    hal.util->persistent_data.scheduler_task = -1;\n\n    _loop_sample_time_us = AP_HAL::micros64();\n    const uint32_t sample_time_us = uint32_t(_loop_sample_time_us);\n    \n    if (_loop_timer_start_us == 0) {\n        _loop_timer_start_us = sample_time_us;\n        _last_loop_time_s = get_loop_period_s();\n    } else {\n        _last_loop_time_s = (sample_time_us - _loop_timer_start_us) * 1.0e-6;', "notes": 'Main-loop timing core: stamps each loop with AP_HAL::micros64() and derives the measured loop time. Drives the cadence of every periodic PNT task (EKF predict/fuse, AHRS, control).'},
            {"num": 6, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_Scheduler/AP_Scheduler.cpp', "lines": '168-176', "line_start": 168, "line_end": 176, "function": 'AP_Scheduler::tick()', "role": 'Source', "code_snippet": 'void AP_Scheduler::tick(void)\n{\n    _tick_counter++;\n    _tick_counter32++;\n}\n\n#if CONFIG_HAL_BOARD == HAL_BOARD_SITL\n/*\n  fill stack with NaN so we can catch use of uninitialised stack', "notes": 'Increments the loop tick counters (_tick_counter / _tick_counter32) that index task scheduling intervals.'},
            {"num": 7, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_Scheduler/AP_Scheduler.h', "lines": '149-155', "line_start": 149, "line_end": 155, "function": 'AP_Scheduler::get_loop_period_us()', "role": 'Transform', "code_snippet": '    // get the time-allowed-per-loop in microseconds\n    uint32_t get_loop_period_us() {\n        if (_loop_period_us == 0) {\n            _loop_period_us = 1000000UL / _loop_rate_hz;\n        }\n        return _loop_period_us;\n    }', "notes": 'Loop-rate→period derivation: _loop_period_us = 1000000UL / _loop_rate_hz. Couples the configured loop rate to the per-loop time budget and to controller/EKF dt.'},
            {"num": 8, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_GPS/AP_GPS.h', "lines": '409-418', "line_start": 409, "line_end": 418, "function": 'AP_GPS::time_week_ms() / time_week()', "role": 'Source', "code_snippet": '    // GPS time of week in milliseconds\n    uint32_t time_week_ms(uint8_t instance) const {\n        return state[instance].time_week_ms;\n    }\n    uint32_t time_week_ms() const {\n        return time_week_ms(primary_instance);\n    }\n\n    // GPS week\n    uint16_t time_week(uint8_t instance) const {', "notes": '[MULTI-CATEGORY] GPS time-of-week (ms-of-week + week number) — the TIMING facet of the GPS_State that also carries Positioning (Table 1 #4/#17). Emitted separately here per the multi-category rule.'},
            {"num": 9, "file_path": 'libraries/AP_HAL/Scheduler.h', "lines": '13-21', "line_start": 13, "line_end": 21, "function": 'AP_HAL::Scheduler::delay() / delay_microseconds()', "role": 'Source', "code_snippet": '    Scheduler() {}\n    virtual void     init() = 0;\n    virtual void     delay(uint16_t ms) = 0;\n\n    /*\n      delay for the given number of microseconds. This needs to be as\n      accurate as possible - preferably within 100 microseconds.\n     */\n    virtual void     delay_microseconds(uint16_t us) = 0;', "notes": 'Abstract HAL timing-service interface (pure virtual; implemented by the board backend — ChibiOS / Linux / SITL). Supplies the time-blocking primitives delay() / delay_microseconds() and the periodic-task registration register_timer_process() / register_io_process() (lines 60-64) on which the main loop is built. Distinct from the AP_Scheduler library (#5-#7) and the AP_HAL::micros()/millis() clock primitives in system.h (#1).'},
